    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`plan_extraction` is implemented in `solution.py` and the test suite passes: `python -m pytest -q tests` gives 49 passed. The one failure on the first run was a mistake in my test: `a/./` normalises to `a`, a valid directory entry, so I moved it to the directory tests. The implementation follows `spec.md`. Dest trailing slashes are stripped, `\\` is a separator, `.` and empty segments are dropped, and `..` pops a segment. Unsafe members (NUL, absolute, drive prefix, climbing above the root, or empty after normalisation) raise `UnsafePathError` before any result is built, so no partial plan is returned. Directory entries are validated and then skipped. Duplicates are detected case-insensitively with `lower()`. The helpers are split out so each function has low cyclomatic complexity. The tests in `tests/test_solution.py` cover those rules, and by inspection every line of `solution.py` is executed. I could not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates here, since only the pytest command was allowed.",
